IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bsma-types`

-- Building (Strata Management) Act 2004 — GOAL 1: IS IT VALIDLY DECIDED?
--
--   "Does this motion carry, as the resolution this matter needs; and was the
--    meeting that decided it called, attended and voted as the Act requires?"
--
-- Source: ../source/BSMA2004.txt — s 2(2)-(8), ss 26, 27, 29-41, 49-50, 53B,
-- 59, 66-67, 70-71, 78, 84-85A, and the First Schedule.

§ `Goal 1 — resolutions and general meetings`

§§ `The six resolutions (s 2(2)-(7))`

-- s 2(2): ordinary — meeting "on the 15th day (or later) after the notice";
-- "(i) if no poll is taken — the number of valid votes counted for the motion
-- are more than the valid votes counted against ...; or (ii) on a poll — the
-- total of the share value ... for ... is more than the total ... against".
-- s 2(3), (5): special and 90% — 22nd day; "on a poll, the total of the share
-- value of the lots for which valid votes are counted for the motion is at
-- least 75% [90%] of the aggregate share value of the lots for which all valid
-- votes are cast". First Schedule para 9(2)(b): a special or 90% resolution is
-- always decided on a poll. s 2(4): unanimous — 22nd day; "supported by every
-- valid vote cast". s 2(6): comprehensive — considered at a meeting on the
-- 22nd day or later, and "at the end of a period of 12 weeks after the general
-- meeting ... at least 90% of the aggregate share value of the lots of all the
-- subsidiary proprietors". s 2(7): by consensus — the same 12 weeks, and "all
-- the subsidiary proprietors ... support the motion in writing".
@ref s 2(2)-(8); First Schedule para 9(2)
GIVEN k IS A `Resolution kind`, m IS A Motion
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the motion is decided as` k `, on` m IF
        m's `a duly convened general meeting`
    AND m's `days from notice to meeting` AT LEAST `the notice days for` k
    AND `the votes carry it`
    WHERE
        `the votes carry it` MEANS
            CONSIDER k
            WHEN `an ordinary resolution` THEN
                IF m's `a poll taken`
                THEN m's `share value of lots with valid votes for` GREATER THAN m's `share value of lots with valid votes against`
                ELSE m's `valid votes for` GREATER THAN m's `valid votes against`
            WHEN `a special resolution` THEN `at least the share of votes cast` 75
            WHEN `a 90% resolution`     THEN `at least the share of votes cast` 90
            WHEN `a unanimous resolution` THEN
                (m's `valid votes against` EQUALS 0) AND (m's `valid votes for` AT LEAST 1)
            WHEN `a comprehensive resolution` THEN
                    m's `weeks since the meeting` AT LEAST 12
                AND (m's `share value voting for, at the end of 12 weeks` TIMES 100) AT LEAST (m's `aggregate share value of all subsidiary proprietors, at the end of 12 weeks` TIMES 90)
            WHEN `a resolution by consensus` THEN
                    m's `weeks since the meeting` AT LEAST 12
                AND m's `every subsidiary proprietor supports it in writing, at the end of 12 weeks`
        `at least the share of votes cast` pct MEANS
            (m's `share value of lots with valid votes for` TIMES 100)
                AT LEAST ((m's `share value of lots with valid votes for` PLUS m's `share value of lots with valid votes against`) TIMES pct)
            AND m's `share value of lots with valid votes for` GREATER THAN 0

-- s 2(2)(a): "the 15th day (or later)"; s 2(3)-(7)(a): "the 22nd day (or later)".
@ref s 2(2)(a)-(7)(a)
GIVEN k IS A `Resolution kind`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the notice days for` k MEANS
    IF k EQUALS `an ordinary resolution` THEN 15 ELSE 22

-- First Schedule para 9(4): on a poll, a vote for a proposed lot is worth
-- "25% of the value ... ignoring any fraction".
@ref First Schedule para 9(3)-(4)
GIVEN `share value` IS A NUMBER, `a proposed lot` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value of the vote, share value` `share value` `, a proposed lot:` `a proposed lot` MEANS
    IF `a proposed lot` THEN FLOOR (`share value` TIMES 25 DIVIDED BY 100) ELSE `share value`

§§ `Which resolution each matter needs`

-- Each matter names its resolution: ss 29(1)(d), 32(3), (3A), 33(1)(a)-(c),
-- 34(1)-(5), 34A(1), 35(1), 37(2), 38(3A), 39(1)-(3), 41(6), (8), (9),
-- 43(3)(a), 50, 54(2)(b), 59, 66(1)(a), (6)(a), 67(3), 70(1), 71(3A), 78(1),
-- 84(1)-(2), 85(1A), 85A(1), (2), (4), (5); First Schedule paras 1A(6), 1C(2).
-- Exclusive use (s 33(1)) and leases (s 34(1)(b), (2)): ordinary up to one
-- year, special over one year and up to 3, 90% over 3. A fixed EV charger
-- lease (s 34A(1)): ordinary up to 10 years; beyond that the Act gives no
-- separate rule and s 34(1)(b) governs (s 34(2A) excludes only s 34A matters).
@ref ss 29(1)(d), 32-35, 34A, 37-39, 41, 43, 50, 54, 59, 66, 67, 70, 71, 78, 84, 85, 85A; First Schedule paras 1A(6), 1C(2)
GIVEN x IS A Matter
GIVETH A `Resolution kind`
`the resolution needed for` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `making, amending or repealing by-laws (s 32(3))`                       THEN `a special resolution`
    WHEN `a by-law for parking lots with fixed EV chargers (s 32(3A))`           THEN `an ordinary resolution`
    WHEN `an exclusive use by-law` y                                             THEN `by term` y
    WHEN `improving common property: facilities, use or structures (s 29(1)(d))` THEN `a special resolution`
    WHEN `transferring common property (s 34(1)(a))`                             THEN `a 90% resolution`
    WHEN `leasing common property` y                                             THEN `by term` y
    WHEN `leasing common property for a fixed EV charger` y                      THEN
        IF y AT MOST 10 THEN `an ordinary resolution` ELSE `a 90% resolution`
    WHEN `accepting land to create additional common property (s 34(3))`         THEN `a special resolution`
    WHEN `approving a subdivision or amalgamation of lots creating common property (s 34(4))` THEN `an ordinary resolution`
    WHEN `amalgamating common property of 2 or more corporations (s 34(5))`      THEN `a special resolution`
    WHEN `granting, accepting or surrendering an easement or restrictive covenant (s 35)` THEN `a unanimous resolution`
    WHEN `authorising an improvement increasing floor area (s 37(2))`            THEN `a 90% resolution`
    WHEN `determining contributions (s 39)`                                      THEN `an ordinary resolution`
    WHEN `levying contributions by a different formula after a change of use (s 41(6))` THEN `a comprehensive resolution`
    WHEN `levying contributions by any other method (s 41(8))`                   THEN `a resolution by consensus`
    WHEN `allowing a discount for early payment (s 41(9))`                       THEN `a special resolution`
    WHEN `selling a lot under a charge for unpaid contributions (s 43(3)(a))`    THEN `a special resolution`
    WHEN `altering or building on common property during the initial period (s 50)` THEN `a special resolution`
    WHEN `removing a council member at a general meeting (s 54(2)(b))`           THEN `an ordinary resolution`
    WHEN `reserving matters to the general meeting (s 59)`                       THEN `an ordinary resolution`
    WHEN `appointing or terminating a managing agent (ss 66(1)(a), (6)(a))`      THEN `an ordinary resolution`
    WHEN `delegating council functions to the managing agent (s 67(3))`          THEN `an ordinary resolution`
    WHEN `an insurance decision under s 71 (s 71(3A))`                           THEN `an ordinary resolution`
    WHEN `not insuring the building under a damage policy (s 70(1))`             THEN `a resolution by consensus`
    WHEN `designating limited common property (s 78(1)(a)(ii), (b))`             THEN `a comprehensive resolution`
    WHEN `terminating the strata scheme (s 84(1))`                               THEN `a resolution by consensus`
    WHEN `dissolving a subsidiary management corporation (s 84(2))`              THEN `a comprehensive resolution`
    WHEN `instituting proceedings or representing subsidiary proprietors (s 85(1A))` THEN `an ordinary resolution`
    WHEN `proceedings or an appeal on a non-lot acquisition (s 85A(1))`          THEN `an ordinary resolution`
    WHEN `claiming compensation on a non-lot acquisition (s 85A(2))`             THEN `an ordinary resolution`
    WHEN `distributing non-lot acquisition compensation (s 85A(4))`              THEN `a special resolution`
    WHEN `asking for the whole land to be acquired (s 85A(5))`                   THEN `a resolution by consensus`
    WHEN `approving a budget for social activities or legal services (s 38(3A))` THEN `an ordinary resolution`
    WHEN `a general meeting on short notice (First Schedule para 1A(6))`         THEN `a special resolution`
    WHEN `holding meetings at a physical place (First Schedule para 1C(2)(b))`   THEN `an ordinary resolution`
    WHERE
        `by term` y MEANS
            BRANCH IF y AT MOST 1 THEN `an ordinary resolution`
                   IF y AT MOST 3 THEN `a special resolution`
                   OTHERWISE           `a 90% resolution`

@ref s 2(2)-(7)
GIVEN x IS A Matter, m IS A Motion
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the matter is validly decided:` x `, on` m IF
    `the motion is decided as` (`the resolution needed for` x) `, on` m

-- First Schedule para 13: "A unanimous resolution, resolution by consensus,
-- comprehensive resolution, 90% resolution or special resolution ... must not
-- be amended or revoked except by a subsequent [resolution of the same kind]".
@ref First Schedule para 13
GIVEN original IS A `Resolution kind`
GIVETH A `Resolution kind`
`the resolution needed to amend or revoke a` original MEANS original

§§ `Who may vote, and the meeting (First Schedule)`

-- First Schedule para 2(1): entitled to vote only if the person is the
-- proprietor, mortgagee in possession or receiver on the strata roll and "has
-- paid ... all contributions and any other moneys"; para 1A(2)(e)(ii): paid
-- "at least 3 days before the commencement of the meeting", except for a
-- unanimous resolution or resolution by consensus. para 2(2): a first
-- mortgagee who votes displaces the proprietor's vote. s 65(9): a person who
-- has not complied with a s 65(8) notice may not vote.
@ref First Schedule paras 1A(2)(e), 2(1)-(2); s 65(9)
GIVEN `on the strata roll` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid up 3 days before` IS A BOOLEAN, `unanimous or consensus` IS A BOOLEAN, `the first mortgagee votes` IS A BOOLEAN, `an outstanding s 65(8) notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proprietor's vote counts, on the roll:` `on the strata roll` `, paid up:` `paid up 3 days before` `, unanimous or consensus:` `unanimous or consensus` `, first mortgagee votes:` `the first mortgagee votes` `, s 65(8) notice outstanding:` `an outstanding s 65(8) notice` IF
        `on the strata roll`
    AND (`paid up 3 days before` OR `unanimous or consensus`)
    AND (NOT `the first mortgagee votes`)
    AND (NOT `an outstanding s 65(8) notice`)

-- First Schedule para 3(2): a quorum is the proprietors "who own at least 30%
-- of the aggregate share value", present in person or by proxy. para 3(3)-(4):
-- if none within half an hour, the meeting may proceed with "2 or more such
-- subsidiary proprietors present in person", but not on a requisition.
@ref First Schedule para 3(2)-(4)
GIVEN present IS A NUMBER, aggregate IS A NUMBER, `minutes after start` IS A NUMBER, `present in person` IS A NUMBER, `convened on requisition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the general meeting may transact business, share value present` present `, aggregate` aggregate `, minutes waited` `minutes after start` `, in person` `present in person` `, on requisition:` `convened on requisition` IF
        (present TIMES 100) AT LEAST (aggregate TIMES 30)
    OR  (    `minutes after start` AT LEAST 30
         AND `present in person` AT LEAST 2
         AND NOT `convened on requisition`)

-- First Schedule para 1A(1): notice "at least 14 days before the meeting";
-- para 1A(6): "if so directed ... by a special resolution", less. The s 2(2)-(7)
-- notice for the motion itself (15 or 22 days) is a separate test, applied in
-- `the motion is decided as` (FORK F2).
@ref First Schedule para 1A(1), (6)
GIVEN `notice given` IS A DATE, meeting IS A DATE, `short notice directed by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the general meeting had enough notice, given` `notice given` `, meeting` meeting `, short notice directed:` `short notice directed by special resolution` IF
    `short notice directed by special resolution` OR (meeting MINUS `notice given`) AT LEAST 14

-- First Schedule para 17(5): a proxy may represent at most "(a) 2 lots; or (b)
-- 2% of the total number of lots ... (rounded down ...), whichever is the
-- higher"; (6): further instruments are void.
@ref First Schedule para 17(5)-(6)
GIVEN lots IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most lots one proxy may represent, lots in the development` lots MEANS
    IF FLOOR (lots TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 100) GREATER THAN 2 THEN FLOOR (lots TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 100) ELSE 2

-- First Schedule para 18(2): proxies lodged "at least 48 hours before" the
-- meeting or poll; s 53B(3)(b)(ii), (4)(a): written nominations and consents
-- "at least 48 hours before the start of the meeting"; para 7(1): the voters'
-- list displayed "at least 48 hours before"; para 3A(3): an adjourned meeting
-- on 14 days' notice.
@ref First Schedule paras 7(1), 18(2); s 53B(3)-(4)
GIVEN `hours before the meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `lodged in time, hours before the meeting` `hours before the meeting` IF
    `hours before the meeting` AT LEAST 48

-- First Schedule para 14(1): a requisition by persons with "at least 20% of
-- the aggregate share value" or "not less than 25% of the total number of
-- subsidiary proprietors" obliges the council to convene an extraordinary
-- general meeting "not later than 6 weeks after" receipt. para 15(1)(b):
-- before the first AGM, 25% of the aggregate share value.
@ref First Schedule paras 14(1), 15(1)(b)
GIVEN `share value signing` IS A NUMBER, aggregate IS A NUMBER, `proprietors signing` IS A NUMBER, proprietors IS A NUMBER, `before the first AGM` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the requisition obliges a meeting, share value` `share value signing` `of` aggregate `, proprietors` `proprietors signing` `of` proprietors `, before the first AGM:` `before the first AGM` IF
    IF `before the first AGM`
    THEN (`share value signing` TIMES 100) AT LEAST (aggregate TIMES 25)
    ELSE    (`share value signing` TIMES 100) AT LEAST (aggregate TIMES 20)
         OR (`proprietors signing` TIMES 100) AT LEAST (proprietors TIMES 25)

-- para 14(1): held "not later than 6 weeks after the receipt"; para 14(3): if
-- not convened "within 14 days after the date of the deposit", the
-- requisitionists may, but the meeting "must not be held after the expiry of
-- 3 months from that date".
@ref First Schedule para 14(1), (3)
GIVEN received IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`a requisitioned meeting must be held by, received` received MEANS received PLUS 42

@ref First Schedule para 14(3)
GIVEN deposited IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`requisitionists may convene from, deposited` deposited MEANS deposited PLUS 15

@ref First Schedule para 14(3)
GIVEN deposited IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`a requisitionists' meeting must be held by, deposited` deposited MEANS `add months` deposited 3

-- First Schedule para 1C(2): wholly virtual only if every member who wishes to
-- take part has access, and the corporation has not resolved otherwise.
@ref First Schedule para 1C(2)
GIVEN `all who wish have access` IS A BOOLEAN, `an ordinary resolution requires a physical place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a general meeting may be held wholly online, access:` `all who wish have access` `, physical place resolved:` `an ordinary resolution requires a physical place` IF
    `all who wish have access` AND NOT `an ordinary resolution requires a physical place`

§§ `When meetings must be held (ss 26, 27; initial period)`

-- s 2(1) "initial period": from constitution "and ending — (a) 12 months
-- later; or (b) on the day when the first annual general meeting ... is held,
-- whichever first occurs".
@ref s 2(1) "initial period"
GIVEN constituted IS A DATE, `first AGM held on` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the initial period ends, constituted` constituted `, first AGM` `first AGM held on` MEANS
    CONSIDER `first AGM held on`
    WHEN JUST a  THEN `the earlier of` a (`add months` constituted 12)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `add months` constituted 12

-- s 26(1): the owner developer must hold the first AGM "no later than the
-- earlier of ... (a) a date that is one month after the end of the initial
-- period ...; (b) a date that is 8 weeks after the owner developer receives a
-- written request from the subsidiary proprietors of at least 10% of the total
-- number of lots".
@ref s 26(1)
GIVEN constituted IS A DATE, `request received` IS A MAYBE DATE, `lots requesting` IS A NUMBER, lots IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the first AGM must be held by, constituted` constituted `, request received` `request received` `, lots requesting` `lots requesting` `of` lots MEANS
    CONSIDER `request received`
    WHEN JUST r  THEN
        IF (`lots requesting` TIMES 100) AT LEAST (lots TIMES 10)
        THEN `the earlier of` `a month after the initial period` (r PLUS 56)
        ELSE `a month after the initial period`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `a month after the initial period`
    WHERE
        `a month after the initial period` MEANS `add months` (`add months` constituted 12) 1

-- s 26(4)(b): the first annual budget is "for a period of 12 months starting on
-- the first day of the month following the date of the first annual general
-- meeting".
@ref s 26(4)(b)
GIVEN `first AGM` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first budget starts on, first AGM` `first AGM` MEANS
    `add months` (Date 1 (DATE_MONTH `first AGM`) (DATE_YEAR `first AGM`)) 1

-- s 27(1): after the first, an AGM "must be held in each calendar year and not
-- more than 15 months after the holding of the last preceding annual general
-- meeting".
@ref s 27(1)
GIVEN last IS A DATE, `next` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the next AGM is in time, last` last `, next` `next` IF
        `next` AT MOST `add months` last 15
    AND DATE_YEAR `next` AT MOST (DATE_YEAR last PLUS 1)

-- s 27(4)-(5): the chairperson and secretary each commit an offence if the next
-- AGM is not held in time, unless they "took all reasonable steps and exercised
-- all due diligence".
@ref s 27(4)-(5)
GIVEN `held in time` IS A BOOLEAN, `all reasonable steps and due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the chairperson and secretary commit an offence, AGM in time:` `held in time` `, due diligence:` `all reasonable steps and due diligence` IF
    (NOT `held in time`) AND (NOT `all reasonable steps and due diligence`)

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

@ref ss 2(1), 26(2)-(10), 27(2)-(3), 53B, First Schedule paras 1, 1B, 3A, 4-12, 16, 19, 20
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`meeting provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "s 2(1): definitions — common property (with its examples), limited common property, lot, proposed lot, owner developer, structural defect and the rest — are read into the facts"
         "s 26(2)-(8), (10): the first AGM's chair, agenda, the documents the developer must deliver, the Commissioner's power to appoint a convenor"
         "s 27(2)-(3): extraordinary general meetings are convened by the council; the First Schedule governs meetings"
         "s 53B: nominations must name the candidate and nominator, with the candidate's consent; withdrawal only in person before the election"
         "First Schedule: notice contents, nomination calls, motions out of order, voting slips and electronic voting, the chairperson, the voters' list, elections, counting, minutes, agenda requisitions, company representatives, the proxy form, and proxies' powers"
